MTS patch: free names and the naming rules (setting mtsFreeNames=1).

Names are taken as spoken (letters only, 2 words of at most 16 letters)
instead of being snapped to the closest entry in firstNames/lastNames.txt,
so Eves can say "I AM <FIRST> <FAMILY>". Naming rules:
- No repeated family names: an Eve naming whose family name a living family
  has, or any family named on this server had (mtsFamilyNames.txt in the run
  dir, so it survives restarts), is refused, and the namer is told "THE
  FAMILY NAME X IS ALREADY TAKEN. CHOOSE A NEW ONE." The agents check the
  same before speaking, against every lineage they ever recorded (all runs).
- Numbered repeat first names: a baby's first name may carry a Roman numeral
  II..X as a second word (YOU ARE AURORA II -> AURORA II DAWN, family DAWN;
  any other second word is dropped as before). A name in use or used
  recently (the curse-name list) gets the next numeral instead of a stock
  first name, and the said phrase shows the numeral.
- Family names outlive their members: when an Eve names her family, her
  living descendants born before the naming get it as their family name,
  and the lineage's name is kept by lineage (Eve) id in
  mtsLineageFamilies.txt (run dir; a world reset deletes it, a new Eve
  with a reused id clears her entry). Forced naming at 8 minutes
  (getLineageLastName) and nameBaby fall back to it, so a child whose
  named relatives all died still gets the family surname, not a random one.
- mtsForceNameSeconds (any mtsFreeNames; default 480 = stock): game seconds
  alive before an unnamed person is force-named (random first name, family
  surname).
With mtsFreeNames=0 (and no mtsForceNameSeconds) everything is stock.

